 "script": {
  "hook": "The phone was offline for an hour. Which messages did it miss?",
  "question": "Design reconnect and catch-up sync for a chat app.",
  "trap": "The trap: reload every conversation on reconnect. It wastes data, and messages sent during the reload still slip through.",
  "steps": [
   "Cursor. Save the last synced sequence number per chat. Ask only for what comes after it.",
   "Gap check. A hole in the sequence means a missed message, so fetch exactly that range.",
   "Backfill. Apply oldest first and dedupe by message id, so retries never double a message.",
   "Handoff. Buffer live messages while catching up, then merge by sequence and go live."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Remember where you stopped. Fetch only the gap, in order.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: Chat list pagination and unread counts.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
